  "body": "## Description:  \nThe `sweep` function in the `BuilderWallet` contract relies on `IERC20.transfer` returning a **boolean** value. This assumption is unsafe for non-standard ERC20 tokens such as USDT, which do not return a **boolean** on `transfer`. When builder fees are distributed in such tokens, the `sweep` call will revert despite the `transfer` succeeding at the token level, causing the withdrawal to fail.\n\n## Impact:  \nIf the underlying asset is a non-standard ERC20, protocol-generated builder fees transferred to the `BuilderWallet` become permanently inaccessible, preventing the builder from withdrawing earned rewards and resulting in fund stuck for the builder who wants to earn fee\n\n**Severity:**  Medium, as protocol-generated builder fees can become permanently inaccessible, preventing the builder from withdrawing earned rewards\n\n## Recommended Mitigation:  \nReplace the raw `IERC20.transfer` call in `sweep` with a safe transfer helper (e.g., `SafeERC20.safeTransfer` or `SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer`) that correctly handles non-standard ERC20 tokens which do not return a boolean value.",
  "proof_of_concept": "1. Create a new file `MockUSDT` at location `test/foundry/MockUSDT.sol` and paste the code:\n(The idea of `MockUSDT` is taken from \"lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/mocks/SafeERC20Helper.sol:ERC20NoReturnMock\" to only replicate the \"no bool return behaviour of USDT on transfer\")\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\ncontract MockUSDT {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    uint256 private _dummy;\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n    }\n\n    // USDT-style: no return value\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) public {\n        balanceOf[msg.sender] -= amount;\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n        _dummy = 0;\n    }\n\n    function transferFrom(address, address, uint256) public {\n        _dummy = 0;\n    }\n\n    function approve(address, uint256) public {\n        _dummy = 0;\n    }\n\n    function allowance(address, address) public pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n2. Create a test file at `test/foundry/BuilderWallet.t.sol` and paste the code:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {BuilderWallet, BuilderFactory} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {MockUSDT} from \"./MockUSDT.sol\";\n\ncontract BuilderWalletTest is Test {\n    BuilderFactory factory;\n    BuilderWallet wallet;\n    MockUSDT mockUSDT;\n\n    address owner;\n    address builderAdmin;\n    address recipient;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        owner = makeAddr(\"OWNER\");\n        builderAdmin = makeAddr(\"BUILDER_ADMIN\");\n        recipient = makeAddr(\"RECIPIENT\");\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        factory = new BuilderFactory(owner);\n\n        address walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(1, builderAdmin);\n        wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        mockUSDT = new MockUSDT();\n\n        mockUSDT.mint(address(wallet), 1_000e6);\n    }\n\n    function testSweepRevertsWithNonStandardERC20() public {\n        vm.startPrank(builderAdmin);\n\n        vm.expectRevert(); // TransferFailed\n        wallet.sweep(address(mockUSDT), recipient);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n```\n3. Run the test",
